      │  ├─ src/review/getReview.ts → review, rest
      │  ├─ src/route/getRoute.ts → route, rest
      │  └─ src/shared/types.ts → route, rest
      ├─ unclaimed: 0
      └─ verdict: holds — every changed file sits in a partition, each with the route spec"
`;

exports[`asRouteGuardPartitionCoverageLines given: [case2] a stone whose override leaves a file unclaimed when: [t0] the coverage is rendered then: it matches the snapshot 1`] = `
"🦉 coverage read — naught written, no review run

🗿 route.guard.partition
   ├─ route = .behavior/v2026_01_01.demo
   ├─ stone = 5.1.execution
   ├─ checked against 2 files changed since main
   └─ scope r2 on 5.1.execution — read by r2
      ├─ partitions
      │  └─ review: 1 narrow target + 0 common targets · ~1,000 tokens of file bodies, ~0 common
      │     └─ src/review/getReview.ts
      ├─ common: 0 (route spec: 0)
      ├─ unclaimed: 1
      │  └─ src/route/getRoute.ts
      ├─ verdict: gap — the entrance gate would halt here
      └─ repair — run this before you arrive
         └─ rhx route.guard.partition --route .behavior/v2026_01_01.demo --for review --peer r2 --stone 5.1.execution \\
              --partition 'review=src/review/**,.behavior/v2026_01_01.demo/**' \\
              --partition 'route=src/route/**,.behavior/v2026_01_01.demo/**' \\
              --mode apply

✨ did you know?
   ├─ claim each domain whole, in every layer, and the files you edit next stay covered
   └─ e.g. src/route/** and blackbox/{,__snapshots__/}driver.route.* in one partition"
`;

